      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your stage 3 kidney disease, you must **not** start taking potassium supplements without first talking to your doctor or a nephrologist. Consuming too much potassium can lead to serious and dangerous heart rhythm problems, which is a significant risk with kidney impairment. Please discuss your fatigue and cramps with your healthcare provider so they can safely check your electrolyte levels and recommend the correct course of action.",
      "source": "target",
